Patch: SR audio layer for the native runtime
Upstream: https://github.com/M-HT/SR at the commit pinned by SR_COMMIT in tools/pipeline.py (games/Albion/SR-Main/Albion-sound.c), as staged by tools/sr_audio.py.
Original: Compare_Samples decides whether a cached sample matches a new one by checking seven sampled 32-bit words of its data, so different samples can compare equal. Panning and volume are computed inline against SDL_mixer. Copies of converted samples keep no unconverted data.
Replacement: Compare_Samples compares every format field and then the full kept original data with memcmp; pan and volume go through the shared Game_AIL_set_sample_pan and Game_AIL_set_sample_volume helpers (runtime/rust/audio.rs); sample copies reserve room for the original data so the comparison has it.
Effect: sample identity no longer depends on a 28-byte signature, and the Rust runtime owns pan and volume so the native mixer and the original Miles calls stay consistent.
Why: the native audio path (runtime/rust/audio.rs) has to share pan and volume state with SR's cached samples.
Evidence: docs/architecture.md; tests/audio_samples.c; the sample-audio regression in the Linux and Wine runs.

